<section class="site-wrap inner-hero"><p class="kicker">WHMCS + SAHDEV CLOUD</p><h1>A small connector.<br>A connected <em>workspace.</em></h1><p>Your hosting records stay in WHMCS. Sahdev runs the AI workflows on its cloud and records usage against the right brand.</p></section>
<div class="site-wrap guide-layout"><nav class="guide-nav" aria-label="Guide contents"><a href="#preview">Release scope</a><a href="#requirements">Requirements</a><a href="#install">Installation</a><a href="#connect">Connect your brand</a><a href="#test">Test a workflow</a><a href="#boundaries">Data & permissions</a></nav><div class="guide-content">
<section id="preview"><p class="kicker">CURRENT RELEASE</p><h2>Acceptance preview.</h2><p>The thin connector currently supports ticket analysis, summarization, draft rewriting, quality scoring and canned-draft generation. All five run their prompts and response processing in SaaS. Staff review the results before using them.</p><p>Live chat, Admin Copilot tools, action approval and rollback, knowledge retrieval, automation, diagnostics, analytics, mobile integration and existing-data migration are still release blockers. The preview must not replace a working standard-module installation.</p><div class="availability-note">Production downloads remain closed until the full migration is verified. Test the acceptance build on a non-production WHMCS installation.</div></section>
<section id="requirements"><h2>Before you begin</h2><ul><li>A working WHMCS installation and an administrator able to configure addon modules.</li><li>A PHP version supported by your WHMCS installation, with cURL, JSON and mbstring. The connector code targets PHP 7.4 or newer.</li><li>Outbound HTTPS connectivity and an accurate server clock.</li><li>A verified SaaS brand, provisioned brand database, credit balance, positive monthly budget and available AI model.</li></ul><p>No public access to your MySQL server is required.</p></section>
<section id="install"><h2>01. Install the connector</h2><p>Back up your WHMCS files and database. Extract the connector archive into the WHMCS root. The entry file must be:</p><code>modules/addons/sahdev_cloud/sahdev_cloud.php</code><p>Open <strong>System Settings → Addon Modules</strong>, activate <strong>Sahdev Cloud Connector</strong>, and explicitly assign the admin roles allowed to use it. The preview uses a separate addon name so it does not overwrite the standard Sahdev module.</p></section>
<section id="connect"><h2>02. Connect a verified brand</h2><ol><li>Create the brand in your SaaS workspace with its exact HTTPS WHMCS URL.</li><li>Add the DNS TXT challenge shown on the brand page, then verify it.</li><li>Wait for HostingSpell to provision the brand database. This is separate from your WHMCS database.</li><li>Issue a one-time enrollment token. Open the connector addon page in WHMCS and enter the cloud URL, installation ID and token.</li></ol><p>Tokens expire after 15 minutes. A new enrollment replaces prior credentials. AI provider keys are configured only in Command Station.</p></section>
<section id="test"><h2>03. Run a staging ticket workflow</h2><p>Open a ticket in a department assigned to your admin account. In the Sahdev Cloud panel, load the available models, choose a workflow and submit. A summary or analysis uses the ticket conversation. Rewrite, score and canned-draft workflows also need a draft.</p><p>Requests are asynchronous. If connectivity fails, use <strong>Check request</strong> to resume the same operation. Copy the resulting draft and review it; the connector never sends it automatically.</p></section>
<section id="boundaries"><h2>What crosses the connection?</h2><p>The current preview sends bounded ticket messages and public staff replies, the ticket reference, basic display context and your editing instruction. It excludes attachments, private notes and credential-table fields. Ticket text can still contain sensitive information; use sanitized staging tickets for acceptance testing.</p><p>Every request is signed and bound to an enrolled brand. WHMCS checks the current admin, addon role, native ticket permission, support department and CSRF token before collecting context. The cloud checks installation identity, plan access, credits and budget before dispatch.</p><p>Core workflow PHP and prompts stay on the server. Connector code and browser UI remain inspectable. The preview exposes no remote SQL endpoint or database mutation workflow. Existing rollback journals stay with the original module until their migration is verified.</p></section>
